  "title": "CHAPTER 3: SECTORS OF THE ECONOMY",
  "order": 223,
  "blocks": [
    {
      "id": "wo1ruco",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. MEANING OF ECONOMIC ACTIVITIES"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Economic activities are broadly classified into Primary, Secondary, and Tertiary sectors based on the nature of activity.",
        "The Primary sector relies directly on natural resources, while the Secondary sector transforms raw materials through manufacturing.",
        "The Tertiary sector provides support services necessary for the functioning of both primary and secondary sectors.",
        "In India, structural transformation has seen GDP contribution shift heavily toward services, while employment remains concentrated in agriculture.",
        "The Organised sector provides job security and formal benefits, whereas the Unorganised sector lacks strict government regulation.",
        "Disguised unemployment is prevalent in agriculture, where extra labor contributes zero marginal productivity."
      ],
      "id": "b2u7h5q"
    },
    {
      "type": "statStrip",
      "stats": [
        {
