    {
      "id": "ki5v7wb",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "3. PRIMARY SECTOR (AGRICULTURE)"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "wua0nzm",
      "content": "Primary sector involves extraction of natural resources directly from earth."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "6c0fyih",
      "content": "Features:<br></br>• Dependent on monsoon<br></br>• Provides raw material<br></br>• Large employment in India<br></br>• Includes allied activities like dairy &amp; fisheries"
    },
    {
      "id": "2omilwr",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "4. SECONDARY SECTOR (INDUSTRY)"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "berwbtg",
      "content": "Secondary sector converts raw materials into finished goods."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "5hjzg8i",
      "content": "Examples: Steel, Textile, Cement, Automobile, Petrochemicals."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "a7492qd",
      "content": "Drives industrialization and infrastructure growth."
    },
    {
      "id": "rfqmxx9",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "5. TERTIARY SECTOR (SERVICES)"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "v8jm8v5",
      "content": "Tertiary sector provides services instead of goods."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "is4q8mn",
      "content": "Examples: Banking, Insurance, IT, Tourism, Healthcare."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "a7x9tix",
      "content": "India is service-dominated economy."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "00q2thh",
      "content": "After 1991 Economic Reforms, India experienced rapid service-led growth."
    },
    {
