    {
      "id": "351v995",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "STRUCTURAL TRANSFORMATION THROUGH PLANS"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "ljmfyjv",
      "content": "India's planning strategy gradually shifted the economy from agriculture-dominated to industry-focused and eventually to service-led growth."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "xksv0ku",
      "content": "• Early Plans → Agriculture focus<br></br>• Mid Plans → Industrial expansion<br></br>• Post-1991 → Service sector boom<br></br>"
    },
    {
      "id": "64ri63b",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "6. SECTOR CONTRIBUTION TO GDP (INDIA)"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "1dcfaeu",
      "content": "• Agriculture – Around 15–17%<br></br>• Industry – Around 28–30%<br></br>• Services – Around 50–55%"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "2w2oyzh",
      "content": "Agriculture employs large population but contributes less to GDP."
    },
    {
