    {
      "id": "2yzujtl",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "12.DISGUISED UNEMPLOYMENT"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "dvjc7fv",
      "content": "Meaning:<br></br>Disguised unemployment refers to a situation where more people are employed than actually required for a given level of output. If some workers are removed, total production does not decrease. In such cases, marginal productivity of additional workers is zero."
    },
    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Competitive exams frequently test the distinction between GDP contribution and employment share across economic sectors in India.",
        "Disguised unemployment features marginal productivity of labor equal to zero and is heavily tested in agriculture-based economics questions.",
        "Differences between Public (welfare-oriented) and Private (profit-oriented) sectors as well as Organised vs. Unorganised labor laws are regular exam topics."
      ],
      "id": "zsrgmou"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "4oi76dj",
      "content": "Example:<br></br>Suppose a farm requires only 4 workers to produce 100 units of wheat, but 8 workers are working on the same farm. Even if 3–4 workers leave, output remains 100 units. This means extra workers were not contributing to production."
    },
    {
      "id": "6te3zis",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Characteristics of Disguised Unemployment"
    },
    {
      "id": "9v6dfur",
      "type": "table",
      "rows": [
        {
          "isHeader": true,
          "cells": [
            "<p><strong>Feature</strong></p>",
            "<p><strong>Explanation</strong></p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Hidden Unemployment</p>",
            "<p>Workers appear employed but are not productive</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Zero Marginal Productivity</p>",
            "<p>Removing extra workers does not reduce output</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Common in Agriculture</p>",
            "<p>Mostly found in rural farming areas</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Low Productivity</p>",
            "<p>Output per worker remains low</p>"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "s8tnvan",
      "content": "Causes:<br></br>• Population pressure on land<br></br>• Small land holdings<br></br>• Lack of industrial jobs<br></br>• Lack of skill diversification"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "k3yrucm",
      "content": "Effects:<br></br>• Low income per capita<br></br>• Poverty<br></br>• Inefficient use of labour<br></br>• Slower economic growth"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "awgi9xk",
      "content": "Solutions:<br></br>• Industrialisation<br></br>• Skill development<br></br>• Rural employment schemes<br></br>• Diversification of rural economy"
    },
    {
      "id": "c1qgpyg",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "13. RRB IMPORTANT ONE-LINERS"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "o9d05ou",
      "content": "• Primary = Extraction<br></br>• Secondary = Manufacturing<br></br>• Tertiary = Services<br></br>• India is service-led economy<br></br>• Agriculture employs most people<br></br>"
    }
  ],
